  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -700,6 +700,15 @@ particular, be very careful when using int8_t, uint8_t, int16_t, or uint16_t\n variables as loop indices; you almost always want to use an \"int\"/\"gint\"\n or \"unsigned\"/\"guint\" as the loop index rather than a shorter type.\n \n+If you want to check if there is reported length left in the buffer and\n+how much, call tvb_reported_length_remaining(tvb, offset) with the current\n+offset each time. That function, like other API functions, checks for overflow\n+and will return 0 if offset is greater than the reported length in the buffer.\n+Retrieving the reported length early on, e.g. at the beginning of a function,\n+and decrementing it in parallel with incrementing the offset can overflow,\n+leading to serious issues. The overhead of an extra function call is worth\n+having one fewer thing to check for overflow yourself.\n+\n If you are fetching a length field from the buffer, corresponding to the\n length of a portion of the packet, and subtracting from that length a\n value corresponding to the length of, for example, a header in the\n",
